## h i g h l i g h t s
A mild one-pot room temperature solution phase method was developed for the large-scale synthesis of trimetallic NiCoCu-based MOF nanosheets.   
The NiCoCu nanosheets with controlled molar ratios have different morphologies, sizes and peroxidaselike catalytic activity.   
 The $(\mathsf{N i}_{2}\mathsf{C o}_{1})_{0.5}\mathsf{C u}_{0.5}$ nanosheets showed the best POD-like catalytic performance toward the reduction of $\mathrm{H}_{2}\mathrm{O}_{2}$ .   
 The $(\mathsf{N i}_{2}\mathsf{C o}_{1})_{0.5}\mathsf{C u}_{0.5}$ nanosheets showed the best antibacterial activity against both $E$ Coli. and MRSA bacteria.   
The ultrathin trimetallic MOF nanosheets can effectually accelerate bacteria-infected wound healing with excellent biocompatibility.
